1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
I don't believe it!

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,050
What's wrong?

3
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,250
Carter Boswell!

4
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,570
Who's Carter Boswell?

5
00:00:06,570 --> 00:00:08,120
He's running for the school board.

6
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:09,520
The election's next month.

7
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,930
What's wrong with wanting to be on the school board?

8
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:13,120
Nothing.

9
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:16,060
But he wants to cut the school budget!

10
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:18,510
Maybe it needs cutting.

11
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:20,460
Cutting the budget is fine,

12
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,640
but he wants to do it

13
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,580
by cutting all the cultural programs.

14
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:24,850
No music, no dance,

15
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,430
no concert, no stage presentations.

16
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,470
Why does he want to do that?

17
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:32,160
He says it's to save the taxpayers' money,

18
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,370
and I think he believes

19
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:35,040
that the taxpayers will vote for him

20
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:38,230
if he spends less on the cultural programs.

21
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:40,130
He's probably right.

22
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:41,660
Lots of people want their taxes

23
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:43,330
used for new books

24
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:46,230
and a new paint job in the schoolrooms.

25
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:48,430
Maybe some of us would like to pay a little bit more

26
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:51,550
and keep the cultural programs for our kids.

27
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:54,290
Well, I'm not sure. Ellen.

28
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:56,580
I hear it from my patients.

29
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:01,850
Lots of people are tired of higher taxes.

30
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:04,010
I know,

31
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:05,120
but if Boswell wins

32
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:06,940
he'll be an important decision-maker

33
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:07,990
on the school board,

34
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:09,190
and he doesn't know anything

35
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:12,040
about our children's education.

36
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:13,030
Who's running against him?

37
00:01:13,030 --> 00:01:15,910
Nobody. That's the problem.

38
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:18,280
Well, it sounds to me like Carter Boswell

39
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,710
is going to win this seat on the board.

40
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:23,080
Oh, not if I can stop him!

41
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:26,150
And how are you going to stop him?

42
00:01:26,150 --> 00:01:28,890
I don't know.

43
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,330
Maybe I'll run against him.

44
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:37,310
Well, you've got my vote.

45
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:39,880
I'm serious, Philip.

46
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,960
Why shouldn't I run?

47
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,230
Why shouldn't you run for what, Mom?

48
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:45,330
Your mother is thinking of

49
00:01:45,330 --> 00:01:47,270
running for the school board.

50
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:49,350
Hey, that's terrific, Mom!

51
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:51,050
Against Carter Boswell?

52
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:52,110
Great!

53
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:53,980
Well, if I run for office,

54
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,890
the voters will have a clear choice.

55
00:01:55,890 --> 00:01:59,170
I stand for everything Boswell doesn't.

56
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:01,620
I think a lot of people will vote for you

57
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,430
against Boswell, Ellen.

58
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:05,640
I'll vote for you.

59
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,580
Will you help me if I do run?

60
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:10,230
Absolutely.

61
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:10,740
The trouble is

62
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:14,470
it takes a little bit of money to run a campaign.

63
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:16,700
I think you can make a difference, Ellen.

64
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:18,120
And in a short campaign

65
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,110
you wouldn't need as much money.

66
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:21,640
You know something, Ellen?

67
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:25,480
Why not give the people of Riverdale a clear choice?

68
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,930
I'm with you.

69
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:34,800
You can make a difference.

70
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:40,570
Come in.

71
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:42,440
Mr. Maxwell?

72
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:45,610
Yes, Charles Maxwell.

73
00:02:45,610 --> 00:02:48,740
My name is Ellen Stewart.

74
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,320
Hello.

75
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:54,990
Please, sit down.

76
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:57,850
You asked to see me.

77
00:02:57,850 --> 00:03:00,200
What would you like to see me about?

78
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,870
I'd like your help.

79
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:04,790
Well,

80
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:08,560
I'm editor of the most influential newspaper in Riverdale.

81
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,400
Actually, it's the only newspaper.

82
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,890
A lot of people would like my help.

83
00:03:12,890 --> 00:03:14,770
Do you have a story?

84
00:03:14,770 --> 00:03:18,030
I'm planning to run for the school board.

85
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,750
Against Carter Boswell?

86
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:21,160
Yes.

87
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,460
Well, that is news.

88
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,160
Will you announce that I'm running?

89
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:29,760
But I need some information.

90
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:31,590
Of course.

91
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:34,590
Why will the voters vote for you against Boswell,

92
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:36,880
Mrs. Stewart?

93
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:40,950
Because I care.

94
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:44,110
"Vote for Ellen Stewart. She cares."

95
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:46,190
Not a bad slogan.

96
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:49,590
But what do you care about?

97
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:52,070
Well, I care about the children of our town.

98
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:53,220
I don't want them to grow up

99
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:57,930
without cultural programs in our school.

100
00:03:57,930 --> 00:04:00,010
Do you have a plan?

101
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:01,320
I want our children to learn

102
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:05,710
more than reading, writing, and arithmetic.

103
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:09,280
I want to keep the after-school programs--

104
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,560
the music, the concerts.

105
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,400
It's not a bad plan.

106
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,290
But who's going to pay for all of this?

107
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:16,530
We are.

108
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:17,940
The citizens of Riverdale, of course.

109
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:22,950
I plan to get help

110
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:25,380
That's fair enough.

111
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:29,480
Exactly what do you want from me, Mrs. Stewart?

112
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,490
You don't know me.

113
00:04:30,490 --> 00:04:33,950
I can't expect you to take my side against Boswell.

114
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:37,830
But I do need some publicity

115
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:38,960
so that the people of our town

116
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,820
know that I'm running for office

117
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:44,510
and that I care about our children.

118
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:46,230
Fair enough.

119
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:48,310
I certainly can print the news.

120
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:51,310
And you are now making news.
